CALIIP — INITIAL PROJECT SETUP

Caliip is a calorie-tracking Progressive Web App (PWA), developed within an 80-hour project.

For now, ONLY initialize the project. Do not implement application features.

SETUP REQUIREMENTS

- Git monorepo using Bun workspaces.
- `apps/web`: Vue 3, TypeScript, Vite, Vuetify 3, Vue Router, Dexie.js, date-fns, vite-plugin-pwa, Vitest.
- `apps/api`: Minimal Bun HTTP server.
- Configure frontend-to-backend communication for local development.
- Add `.gitignore`, `.env.example`, and a basic README.
- Ensure both applications start successfully.

CONSTRAINTS

- Use Vuetify for styling, no Tailwind.
- Use Vue composables, no Pinia.
- Use native Fetch, no Axios.
- Keep the setup minimal and avoid unnecessary dependencies.
- Do not implement meal CRUD, database tables, AI recognition, or USDA integration yet.
- Never commit API keys.

Read the existing architecture, data schema, Dexie implementation, and technology decisions files before making changes.

GOAL

A working frontend and backend scaffold, ready for feature development.